    "result_text": "The build is green. There's a single test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes along with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-duplicate (\"possible duplicate\") detection on `POST /api/owners`. When a new owner is **not** a hard (identity-key) duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a **different** telephone, it is still created and flagged.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes them: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32 owner id).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added persistent `possible_duplicate` (Boolean) and `possible_duplicate_of` (Integer) columns with getters/setters. MapStruct auto-maps these to the DTO by name.\n\n3. **Schema SQL** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the matching `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns to the `owners` table. (Tests run on `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in the schema.)\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after the existing hard-duplicate 409 check, it calls a new `findPossibleDuplicate(owner)` helper and sets `possibleDuplicate = (match != null)` and `possibleDuplicateOf = match.id` (or null). The helper matches an existing owner with the same `lastName` (case-insensitive) and `postcode` but a different normalized telephone, picking the lowest id for determinism. Owners without a postcode never soft-match.\n\nThe check runs after the hard-duplicate rejection, so identity-key duplicates are still 409'd; only the softer last-name/postcode overlap is flagged.",
