        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change fits the codebase's established structure cleanly:\n\n- `findPossibleDuplicate` mirrors the existing private-helper idiom in this controller exactly \u2014 `countNamesakes`, `countOwnersInCity`, `countOwnersRegisteredOn`, and especially `isIdentityKeyInUse` all follow the same \"stream over `clinicService.findAllOwners()` and filter\" shape. Placing it directly after `isIdentityKeyInUse` (its conceptual sibling \u2014 hard vs. soft duplicate) is the natural home.\n- The wiring in `addOwner` sits right alongside the analogous `setNamesakeCount`/`setBulkSignupWarning` derivations, keeping all the \"compute derived flags before save\" logic together and in a sensible order (after the hard-duplicate 409, as the Javadoc notes).\n- The `Owner` model additions follow the existing field + getter/setter convention next to the comparable `bulkSignupWarning` field.\n- Schema changes are applied consistently across all four dialects (h2/hsqldb/mysql/postgres), and the OpenAPI additions match the verbose, `readOnly` style of the surrounding derived properties.\n- No new imports needed (`Comparator` already present), no duplication introduced, and no unit is being turned into a catch-all \u2014 the helper carries a single, well-scoped responsibility.\n\nA maintainer of this codebase would find this natural and consistent with the surrounding conventions."
